# Fast local-dev profile.
#
# NOTE: As of the single-service / automine rework, the DEFAULT stack is
# already fast -- you no longer need this file for speed:
#
#   docker compose --profile aztec up
#
# Why the default is fast now:
#  - The `aztec` service runs its own AUTOMINE anvil (no --block-time) in the
#    same container. Automine activates the node's AnvilTestWatcher, which
#    warps each L2 slot forward ~2 s after a tx is pending instead of idling a
#    full wall-clock slot (~22 s). The old slot-tuning knobs
#    (AZTEC_SLOT_DURATION / ETHEREUM_SLOT_DURATION / ANVIL_BLOCK_TIME /
#    SEQ_L1_PUBLISHING_TIME_ALLOWANCE_IN_SLOT) no longer apply -- there is no
#    fixed-cadence external L1 to fit a publishing window into.
#  - Proverless is the default (PXE_PROVER_ENABLED=false, PXE_PROVER=none): a
#    real ClientIVC proof costs ~4 s/tx and is never required on a local
#    network (the node already runs realProofs=false).
#
# This file is kept only so the documented
#   docker compose --env-file .env.fast --profile aztec up
# command still works; it simply pins the now-default proverless values.

PXE_PROVER_ENABLED=false
PXE_PROVER=none
GOVERNANCE_VOTING_WINDOW_BLOCKS=5
WALLET_MIN_FEE_PADDING=30

# ---- Proving-realism override (slow) -----------------------------------------
# To exercise client-side ClientIVC proving (testnet-like), flip these on:
# PXE_PROVER_ENABLED=true
# PXE_PROVER=
